<tt xmlns="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml" xmlns:itunes="http://music.apple.com/lyric-ttml-internal" xmlns:ttm="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml#metadata" itunes:timing="Word" xml:lang="ko" xmlns:amll="http://www.example.com/ns/amll"><head><metadata><ttm:agent type="person" xml:id="v1"/><iTunesMetadata xmlns="http://music.apple.com/lyric-ttml-internal" leadingSilence="0"><translations><translation type="subtitle" xml:lang="en-US"><text for="L1">Where I'll lie down one day</text><text for="L2">It's probably much higher up</text><text for="L3">No, I don't want to take root</text><text for="L4">In a sleek, just-right kind of place</text><text for="L5">Stick close, right behind me</text><text for="L6">Line up clean</text><text for="L7">I'm determined to bloom in the sky</text><text for="L8">Mm, what a tiny leader</text><text for="L9">Teetering at the edge</text><text for="L10">A holssi drifting toward</text><text for="L11">Another path</text><text for="L12">Fly high to bloom</text><text for="L13">If someone asks</text><text for="L14">How I've been lately</text><text for="L15">Please tell them</text><text for="L16">"She became a holssi"</text><text for="L17">Follow me, I'm gonna go to win</text><text for="L18">Follow me, flying to the top</text><text for="L19">You say "whoo"</text><text for="L20">I may fly</text><text for="L21">You say "whoo"</text><text for="L22">Then I fly</text><text for="L23">Follow me, even without wings</text><text for="L24">Follow me, rising up into the air</text><text for="L25">You say "whoo"</text><text for="L26">I may fly</text><text for="L27">You say "whoo"</text><text for="L28">Then I fly</text><text for="L29">I'll fly right through the center, so the world can see me</text><text for="L30">Better bring your sunglasses to protect your eyes</text><text for="L31">Look up and it blinds</text><text for="L32">No fear of heights, none of that fright</text><text for="L33">I rise way too close to the burning sun</text><text for="L34">From up, I'll look down with a calm stare</text><text for="L35">Choose a cloud to hop on</text><text for="L36">It's been a while, so</text><text for="L37">Shall I bring the ruckus?</text><text for="L38">Spinning, twirling, I'm a</text><text for="L39">Holssi, riding the</text><text for="L40">Steep wind</text><text for="L41">Fly high to bloom</text><text for="L42">If someone asks</text><text for="L43">How I've been lately</text><text for="L44">Please tell them</text><text for="L45">"She became a holssi"</text><text for="L46">Follow me, I'm gonna go to win</text><text for="L47">Follow me, flying to the top</text><text for="L48">You say "whoo"</text><text for="L49">I may fly</text><text for="L50">You say "whoo"</text><text for="L51">Then I fly</text><text for="L52">Follow me, even without wings</text><text for="L53">Follow me, rising up into the air</text><text for="L54">You say "whoo"</text><text for="L55">I may fly</text><text for="L56">You say "whoo"</text><text for="L57">Then I fly</text><text for="L58">Even if the road ahead gets rough</text><text for="L59">No whining, leave it behind</text><text for="L60">This was my choice, like always</text><text for="L61">The chances it'll be easy is zero</text><text for="L62">I'll shake off every last thing left</text><text for="L63">Wish you luck everyone</text><text for="L64">I'll still bow and say goodbye</text><text for="L65">May god be with ya</text><text for="L66">See ya</text></translation></translations><songwriters><songwriter>Chaekyu Lee</songwriter><songwriter>IU</songwriter><songwriter>John Lee</songwriter></songwriters><transliterations><transliteration automaticallyCreated="true" xml:lang="ko-Latn"><text for="L1"><span begin="10.840" end="11.333" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml">nae ga</span>  <span begin="11.333" end="11.698" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml">nu ul</span>  <span begin="11.698" end="12.438" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml">ja rin</span>  <span begin="12.438" end="13.492" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml">a ma do</span></te